  "question": {
    "text": "The kinetic energy of a satellite in its orbit around the earth is E . What should be the kinetic energy of the satellite so as to enable it to escape from the gravitational pull of the earth?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sLpWY",
      "text": "$4 E$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fNt46",
      "text": "2 E",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "8u2rW",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{E}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vgPT7",
      "text": "E",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know that $v_e=\\sqrt{2} v_0$, where $\\mathrm{v}_0$ is orbital velocity.\nK.E. in the orbit, $E=\\frac{1}{2} M v_0{ }^2$\nK.E. to escape $E=\\frac{1}{2} M v_e^2=\\frac{1}{2} M\\left(2 v_0{ }^2\\right)$\n$=\\frac{1}{2} M v_0^2 \\times 2=2 E$",
    "image": null
  },
